  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Why GraphQL Explodes: The N+1 Problem",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The N+1 Shape",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "One query loads N parents, then N follow-up queries load each parent's child — N+1 round trips where 2 would do. GraphQL executes per field, not per query, so nesting multiplies resolver calls."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{ posts(first: 50) {   # 1 query",
            "    author { name }    # + 50 queries",
            "  }",
            "}                      # = 51 trips"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Why It Is The Default Here"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "REST hides it behind hand-written endpoints",
            "Clients pick the shape at runtime",
            "Join set is unknown until the query arrives",
            "50 posts by 5 authors still fires 50 queries"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Depth Multiplies"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`posts`, `author`, `company`, `employees` = 1+50+50+50N",
            "Depth multiplies the count, it never just adds",
            "Doubling `first:` doubles queries linearly",
            "ORMs share it: ActiveRecord, Hibernate, Django"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Latency Math",
          "items": [
            "51 queries × 8ms round trip = 408ms of wait",
            "Each query itself: 0.2ms indexed lookup",
            "Same rows via one `IN` query: about 10ms",
            "Round-trip count is the bill, not the rows"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Log Signature"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "log",
          "lines": [
            "req=8f2 SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=? -- 3",
            "req=8f2 SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=? -- 7",
            "req=8f2 ...48 more, same request id"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Client asks",
            "Queries",
            "Wall time"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`first: 10`",
              "11",
              "88ms"
            ],
            [
              "`first: 50`",
              "51",
              "408ms"
            ],
            [
              "`first: 100`",
              "101",
              "808ms"
            ],
            [
              "one `IN`",
              "2",
              "~16ms"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Eager-loading everything wastes unasked work",
            "Fewer resolvers is not the fix",
            "Defer each load, then group them"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Trips, Not Rows",
          "text": "The database is rarely the bottleneck — the number of round trips is. The same rows in one statement cost 10ms."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Every Field Has A Resolver",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "author: (parent, args, ctx, info) => {...}",
            "// field with no resolver gets this one:",
            "const dflt = (parent) => parent[fieldName]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`parent` is the resolved value one level up",
            "`context` is built once per request, passed to all",
            "`info` carries AST, field path, return type",
            "Basis for lookahead and projection tricks"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "How Resolvers Execute & Meet DataLoader",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Tree Walk"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "query root",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
