    },
    {
      "page_title": "Lookahead, Compiled SQL & Unbounded Rows",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Lookahead"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read `info`, project requested fields into one JOIN",
            "Wins on round trips, loses on complexity",
            "You duplicate the schema shape by hand",
            "Two one-to-many edges return N×M rows",
            "DataLoader never multiplies rows"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Generated Layers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Join Monster, Prisma, Hasura, PostGraphile compile AST to SQL",
            "Least code written, least control kept",
            "Prisma batches `findUnique` calls automatically",
            "Always `include: {author: true}` over-fetches"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Per Entity, Per Level"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "DataLoader still issues one query per level per entity type — batching, not elimination. Lookahead collapses those levels into a single statement, at the price of hand-written projection."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Side By Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "DataLoader",
                "lines": [
                  "batch by key",
                  "per-request cache",
                  "ORM-agnostic",
                  "D round trips"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "JOIN lookahead",
                "lines": [
                  "one statement",
                  "row multiplication",
                  "hand-written",
                  "hot paths only"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Different Axis",
          "items": [
            "Persisted queries and `@defer`: client trips only",
            "Neither touches server-side N+1",
            "Redis, `@cacheControl`, CDN: across requests",
            "DataLoader helps inside one request only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Default, Then Tune",
          "text": "DataLoader first because it is correct everywhere. Add lookahead only on proven hot paths — they compose: lookahead the top list, DataLoader whatever the projection missed."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rows Are Still Unbounded",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Batching Bounds Trips Only",
          "text": "`{a{b{c{d{e}}}}}` with `first: 100` at each level is millions of rows in a handful of batches. Flexibility is a DoS surface: one small string, unbounded work."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
